- AN-23 (system): Fact-check (supported): All three components of the claim are substantiated by web search results. Oak Ridge workers were injected with plutonium without consent (documented case of Ebb Cade on April 10, 1945). Hanford communities experienced intentional and unintentional radioactive releases. An April 17, 1947 Atomic Energy Commission memo explicitly ordered classification of human experiment documents to prevent adverse public opinion and legal suits.
